 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "As-Sa'di's «الكفر والفسوق والعصيان» (49:7 word for word) is not used. Coins for «ويقبضون أيديهم» and «أموالا»; wind for the fleeting enjoyment. Nothing drawn for the Fire (68). STAGING v4: c1 (67): a town by day; two small groups of three men (the hypocrites; the hypocrite women of the verse are not drawn as figures) come together (the right group walks in: they are of one another, As-Sa'di: allies of each other); they speak to each other on 67:6 and 67:8 (enjoining wrong, forbidding good) and the left group shakes its head on 67:10 (the good); a coins plate undraws on 67:11-13 (they close their hands from charity: both tafsirs) as they turn away on 67:12 and 67:13 (forgetting Allah). c2 (68) stays ambient (the Fire). c3 (69): a market by day: an uncountable crowd plate for the nations before them (69:1), a coins plate for their wealth (69:8); the past nations themselves and any ruin are not drawn. The hypocrites sit in the market (their enjoyment of their share: As-Sa'di, taking it with pleasure); the right group walks in and sits down on 69:13; they talk on 69:21 and 69:23 (indulging in falsehood: both tafsirs, falsehood and lying); a falling-leaf plate on 69:25 (their deeds come to nothing). The cover now shows the two groups (67:8)."
 },
